<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">West Indies Federation</h1><p class="st-meta">1958 CE – 1962 CE · capital Port of Spain</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Britain's attempt to lead its Caribbean colonies to independence as one nation, which broke up after only four years when Jamaica voted to leave.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Discussions on federation began at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montego-bay">Montego Bay</a> in 1947. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation came into being on 3 January 1958, joining ten British territories: <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trinidad-and-tobago">Trinidad and Tobago</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barbados">Barbados</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-antigua">Antigua</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-christopher-nevis-anguilla">Saint Kitts-Nevis-Anguilla</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/montserrat">Montserrat</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windward-islands">Windward Islands</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grenada">Grenada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-vincent-island">Saint Vincent</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-lucia">Saint Lucia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commonwealth-of-dominica">Dominica</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The federal government, led by Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grantley-adams">Grantley Adams</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barbados">Barbados</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patrick-buchan-hepburn-1st-baron-hailes">Lord Hailes</a> as governor-general, sat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-spain">Port of Spain</a>, as the chosen capital site at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaguaramas">Chaguaramas</a> was a US base. It had a small budget, no power over income tax and no <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/customs-union">customs union</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jamaica">Jamaica</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a>, the largest members, feared paying for the small islands and disagreed over free movement of people.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Jamaicans voted to leave in a referendum in September 1961, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-williams">Eric Williams</a> declared that 'one from ten leaves nought'. The federation was dissolved on 31 May 1962. Shared institutions such as the University of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> and the West Indies cricket team survived, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean-community">CARICOM</a> later revived regional cooperation.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/west-indies-federation.jpg" alt="West Indies Federation" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Stepshep · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_West_Indies_Federation_(1958%E2%80%931962).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1958 CE – 1962 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Port of Spain</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Grantley Adams, Lord Hailes</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism and Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, <a href="/countries/trinidad-and-tobago">Trinidad and Tobago</a>, <a href="/countries/barbados">Barbados</a>, <a href="/countries/grenada">Grenada</a>, <a href="/countries/saint-lucia">Saint Lucia</a>, <a href="/countries/dominica">Dominica</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Federation of the West Indies</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=west-indies-federation" aria-label="West Indies Federation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2985 1780 64